{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"09d27a55e23f0042ba096ed63e33a748cb4e944e664ac5e7d437375198cfe694","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar doctor command - mapping configuration","key_entities":["src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py","mapping_config.load_mapping_config","MappingConfigError","mapping_probe.build_probe","config.projects","effective_status_map","effective_type_map","effective_link_map","assert_type_decisions_complete","capability_installed","jira_datacenter","JIRA_PAT","resolve_jira_datacenter_settings","tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor.py","docs/user-guide.md"],"problem_keywords":["mapping configuration diagnostics","offline validation","live drift detection","config errors","portability"],"propositions":["Offline mapping config validation must detect and report internally-invalid configs (non-integer hierarchy, malformed vocabulary blocks, out-of-vocabulary values, unmapped-non-skipped entries) as error findings with the MappingConfigError message verbatim, via provider-neutral resolvers without Jira import","Live drift detection between configured and observed Jira vocabulary (status, type, link) must be a best-effort check that degrades gracefully to an unavailable finding when the jira-datacenter extra is absent, credentials are unset, settings resolution fails, or the probe transport times out (doctor-side bounded to 10s)","The mapping diagnostics function must operate as a separate findings list in doctor.scan(), rendered and folded into exit code but excluded from run_repair iteration, preserving the blocking-edge finding contract","All-empty projects.<KEY> stub blocks must yield warning findings (non-fatal), while all error-class problems must yield error findings and non-zero exit","Hierarchy divergence detection is excluded from live drift checks because the Data Center probe never observes hierarchyLevel (Cloud-only), though offline hierarchy validation via MappingConfigError still covers invalid hierarchy values"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787475416215275001,"uuid":"a46f8e15-59dd-41ec-a7fb-12c4039b1bac"}